.TH EUCLID-CLI-EDS-UPDATE-ZONE 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.3.2" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eds-update-zone \- change a zone's TTL or description
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eds update-zone
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I ZONE
[\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-description\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fITEXT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Changes what a zone says about itself: its TTL, its description, or
both. Only what is given changes \- setting the TTL leaves the
description as it was, and the other way round. At least one of the two
has to be given.
.PP
The zone's TTL is used by every record in it that sets none of its own,
and is how long a resolver may cache an answer saying a name or a type
is not there. A changed TTL is answered by the server within a moment;
resolvers that cached an answer under the old TTL keep it until that
runs out. Lowering it a while before a planned change is how to make
the change land quickly everywhere.
.PP
Every update moves the zone's SOA serial, the TTL being part of the
SOA.
.PP
A zone cannot be renamed or moved to another namespace: its name is
what its records and every grant on it refer to. To rename one, create
the new zone, put its records, and delete the old one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fIZONE\fR
The zone's apex. Required.
.TP
.BR \-\-ttl " " \fISECONDS\fR
New TTL, at least 1 and at most 2147483647. Unlike
.BR euclid-cli-eds-create-zone (1),
0 does not mean the default here; it is refused.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-description " " \fITEXT\fR
New description.
.I \(dq\(dq
clears it.
.SH OUTPUT
The zone as it now is, as JSON, in the form
.BR euclid-cli-eds-get-zone (1)
shows it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The zone was updated.
.TP
.B 1
Neither option was given, no such zone in your account (HTTP 404), the
TTL is out of range, or a grant does not allow it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eds update-zone --name corp.example --ttl 60
euclid-cli eds update-zone --name corp.example --description "office network"
euclid-cli eds update-zone --name lab.corp.example --description ""
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eds (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-get-zone (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-create-zone (1)
